{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Hotkeys includes three hooks for tracking the real-time state of keyboard keys. Use them to show modifier state in the UI or to build hold-to-activate features."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"useheldkeys","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useHeldKeys"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns a reactive array of all currently held key names."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useHeldKeys } from '@tanstack/preact-hotkeys'\n\nfunction KeyDisplay() {\n  const heldKeys = useHeldKeys()\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      {heldKeys.length > 0\n        ? `Held: ${heldKeys.join(' + ')}`\n        : 'No keys held'}\n    </div>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The returned array contains key names like "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'Shift'"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'Control'"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'Meta'"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'A'"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'ArrowUp'"},{"type":"text","value":", etc. Keys appear in the order they were pressed."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"useheldkeycodes","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useHeldKeyCodes"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns a reactive object mapping held key names to their physical key codes ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"event.code"},{"type":"text","value":" values). This is useful when you need to distinguish between left and right modifiers."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useHeldKeyCodes } from '@tanstack/preact-hotkeys'\n\nfunction KeyCodeDisplay() {\n  const heldCodes = useHeldKeyCodes()\n  // Example: { Shift: \"ShiftLeft\", Control: \"ControlRight\" }\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      {Object.entries(heldCodes).map(([key, code]) => (\n        <div key={key}>\n          {key}: {code}\n        </div>\n      ))}\n    </div>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"usekeyhold","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useKeyHold"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Checks whether a specific key is currently held. This hook is optimized to only trigger re-renders when the specified key's held state changes, not when other keys are pressed or released."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useKeyHold } from '@tanstack/preact-hotkeys'\n\nfunction ModifierIndicators() {\n  const isShiftHeld = useKeyHold('Shift')\n  const isCtrlHeld = useKeyHold('Control')\n  const isAltHeld = useKeyHold('Alt')\n  const isMetaHeld = useKeyHold('Meta')\n\n  return (\n    <div className=\"modifier-bar\">\n      <span className={isShiftHeld ? 'active' : ''}>Shift</span>\n      <span className={isCtrlHeld ? 'active' : ''}>Ctrl</span>\n      <span className={isAltHeld ? 'active' : ''}>Alt</span>\n      <span className={isMetaHeld ? 'active' : ''}>Meta</span>\n    </div>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"common-patterns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Common patterns"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"reading-held-keys-inside-a-stable-callback","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reading held keys inside a stable callback"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useKeyHold"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useHeldKeys"},{"type":"text","value":" return the state for the current render. If a memoized callback reads those values, include them in its dependencies so it sees updates."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For an event handler that should read the latest held keys without subscribing to render updates, use the existing "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getKeyStateTracker()"},{"type":"text","value":" API:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useCallback } from 'preact/hooks'\nimport { getKeyStateTracker } from '@tanstack/preact-hotkeys'\n\nfunction KeyInspector() {\n  const tracker = getKeyStateTracker()\n  const logHeldKeys = useCallback(() => {\n    console.log(tracker.getHeldKeys())\n    console.log('Space held:', tracker.isKeyHeld('Space'))\n  }, [tracker])\n\n  return <button type=\"button\" onClick={logHeldKeys}>Log held keys</button>\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The tracker is a shared singleton, so its identity stays stable during normal use. Initialize it while setting up the component, before the keys you want to observe are pressed. Read "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getHeldKeys()"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isKeyHeld()"},{"type":"text","value":" inside the callback; saving their return values outside the callback would save an earlier snapshot. These imperative reads do not subscribe the component to updates. Use the hooks when held keys affect rendering, and do not destroy the shared tracker when a component unmounts."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For a mouse or wheel handler that only needs a modifier's state for that event, read the event's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ctrlKey"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"shiftKey"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"altKey"},{"type":"text","value":", or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"metaKey"},{"type":"text","value":" property directly:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useCallback } from 'preact/hooks'\nimport type { JSX } from 'preact'\n\nfunction WheelInspector() {\n  const onWheel = useCallback((event: JSX.TargetedWheelEvent<HTMLDivElement>) => {\n    if (event.ctrlKey) {\n      console.log('Wheel event with Control modifier')\n    }\n  }, [])\n\n  return <div onWheel={onWheel}>Scroll here</div>\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This reads the modifier state reported by the event. Browsers can also report "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ctrlKey"},{"type":"text","value":" for a trackpad pinch gesture, so it does not necessarily mean the physical Control key is held."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"hold-to-reveal-ui","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Hold-to-reveal UI"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Show additional options while a modifier is held:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useKeyHold } from '@tanstack/preact-hotkeys'\n\nfunction FileItem({ file }: { file: File }) {\n  const isShiftHeld = useKeyHold('Shift')\n\n  return (\n    <div className=\"file-item\">\n      <span>{file.name}</span>\n      {isShiftHeld && (\n        <button className=\"danger\" onClick={() => permanentlyDelete(file)}>\n          Permanently Delete\n        </button>\n      )}\n      {!isShiftHeld && (\n        <button onClick={() => moveToTrash(file)}>\n          Move to Trash\n        </button>\n      )}\n    </div>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"keyboard-shortcut-hints","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keyboard shortcut hints"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Display different shortcut hints based on which modifiers are held:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useKeyHold } from '@tanstack/preact-hotkeys'\n\nfunction ShortcutHints() {\n  const isModHeld = useKeyHold('Meta') // or 'Control' on Windows\n\n  if (!isModHeld) return null\n\n  return (\n    <div className=\"shortcut-overlay\">\n      <div>S - Save</div>\n      <div>Z - Undo</div>\n      <div>Shift+Z - Redo</div>\n      <div>K - Command Palette</div>\n    </div>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"debugging-key-display","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Debugging key display"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Combine hooks with formatting utilities for a rich debugging display:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  useHeldKeys,\n  useHeldKeyCodes,\n  formatForDisplay,\n  type RegisterableHotkey,\n} from '@tanstack/preact-hotkeys'\n\nfunction KeyDebugger() {\n  const heldKeys = useHeldKeys()\n  const heldCodes = useHeldKeyCodes()\n\n  return (\n    <div className=\"key-debugger\">\n      <h3>Active Keys</h3>\n      {heldKeys.map((key) => (\n        <div key={key}>\n          <strong>\n            {formatForDisplay(key as RegisterableHotkey, { useSymbols: true })}\n          </strong>\n          <span className=\"code\">{heldCodes[key]}</span>\n        </div>\n      ))}\n      {heldKeys.length === 0 && <p>Press any key...</p>}\n    </div>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"platform-quirks","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Platform quirks"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The underlying "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"KeyStateTracker"},{"type":"text","value":" handles several platform-specific issues:"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"macos-modifier-key-behavior","children":[{"type":"text","value":"macOS modifier key behavior"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"On macOS, when a modifier key is held and a non-modifier key is pressed, the OS sometimes swallows the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"keyup"},{"type":"text","value":" event for the non-modifier key. TanStack Hotkeys detects and handles this automatically so held key state stays accurate."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"window-blur","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Window blur"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When the browser window loses focus, the tracker clears all held keys. This prevents \"stuck\" keys that would otherwise appear held even after the user tabs away and releases them."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"under-the-hood","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Under the hood"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"All three hooks subscribe to the singleton "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"KeyStateTracker"},{"type":"text","value":" via "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/preact-store"},{"type":"text","value":". The tracker manages its own event listeners on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"document"},{"type":"text","value":" and maintains state in a TanStack Store, which the hooks subscribe to reactively."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { getKeyStateTracker } from '@tanstack/preact-hotkeys'\n\nconst tracker = getKeyStateTracker()\n\n// Imperative access (also available inside callbacks)\ntracker.getHeldKeys()        // string[]\ntracker.isKeyHeld('Shift')   // boolean\ntracker.isAnyKeyHeld(['Shift', 'Control']) // boolean\ntracker.areAllKeysHeld(['Shift', 'Control']) // boolean","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"modifier-held-shortcut-hints","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Modifier-held shortcut hints"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useHotkeyHint"},{"type":"text","value":" answers whether held modifiers are relevant to a binding. Keep formatting and badge styling in your component:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const visible = useHotkeyHint('Alt+Shift+[KeyK]')","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Alt+Shift+[KeyK]"},{"type":"text","value":", holding Alt, Shift, or both reveals the hint. An extra Control hides it; releasing all modifiers or blurring the window hides it. Nonmodifier keys are ignored. AltGraph does not reveal hints. Pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ exact: true }"},{"type":"text","value":" to require all binding modifiers, or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ platform: 'mac' }"},{"type":"text","value":" to resolve Mod explicitly. Supply the same platform used by the registration when overriding detection."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Combine the boolean with the action's enabled state. The helper does not register a shortcut or determine whether its target is focused. The core equivalent is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"matchesHeldModifiers(binding, heldKeys, options)"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"useheldkeys","text":"useHeldKeys","level":2},{"id":"useheldkeycodes","text":"useHeldKeyCodes","level":2},{"id":"usekeyhold","text":"useKeyHold","level":2},{"id":"common-patterns","text":"Common patterns","level":2},{"id":"reading-held-keys-inside-a-stable-callback","text":"Reading held keys inside a stable callback","level":3},{"id":"hold-to-reveal-ui","text":"Hold-to-reveal UI","level":3},{"id":"keyboard-shortcut-hints","text":"Keyboard shortcut hints","level":3},{"id":"debugging-key-display","text":"Debugging key display","level":3},{"id":"platform-quirks","text":"Platform quirks","level":2},{"id":"macos-modifier-key-behavior","text":"macOS modifier key behavior","level":3},{"id":"window-blur","text":"Window blur","level":3},{"id":"under-the-hood","text":"Under the hood","level":2},{"id":"modifier-held-shortcut-hints","text":"Modifier-held shortcut hints","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nTanStack Hotkeys includes three hooks for tracking the real-time state of keyboard keys. Use them to show modifier state in the UI or to build hold-to-activate features.\n\n## `useHeldKeys`\n\nReturns a reactive array of all currently held key names.\n\n```tsx\nimport { useHeldKeys } from '@tanstack/preact-hotkeys'\n\nfunction KeyDisplay() {\n  const heldKeys = useHeldKeys()\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      {heldKeys.length > 0\n        ? `Held: ${heldKeys.join(' + ')}`\n        : 'No keys held'}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nThe returned array contains key names like `'Shift'`, `'Control'`, `'Meta'`, `'A'`, `'ArrowUp'`, etc. Keys appear in the order they were pressed.\n\n## `useHeldKeyCodes`\n\nReturns a reactive object mapping held key names to their physical key codes (`event.code` values). This is useful when you need to distinguish between left and right modifiers.\n\n```tsx\nimport { useHeldKeyCodes } from '@tanstack/preact-hotkeys'\n\nfunction KeyCodeDisplay() {\n  const heldCodes = useHeldKeyCodes()\n  // Example: { Shift: \"ShiftLeft\", Control: \"ControlRight\" }\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      {Object.entries(heldCodes).map(([key, code]) => (\n        <div key={key}>\n          {key}: {code}\n        </div>\n      ))}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n## `useKeyHold`\n\nChecks whether a specific key is currently held. This hook is optimized to only trigger re-renders when the specified key's held state changes, not when other keys are pressed or released.\n\n```tsx\nimport { useKeyHold } from '@tanstack/preact-hotkeys'\n\nfunction ModifierIndicators() {\n  const isShiftHeld = useKeyHold('Shift')\n  const isCtrlHeld = useKeyHold('Control')\n  const isAltHeld = useKeyHold('Alt')\n  const isMetaHeld = useKeyHold('Meta')\n\n  return (\n    <div className=\"modifier-bar\">\n      <span className={isShiftHeld ? 'active' : ''}>Shift</span>\n      <span className={isCtrlHeld ? 'active' : ''}>Ctrl</span>\n      <span className={isAltHeld ? 'active' : ''}>Alt</span>\n      <span className={isMetaHeld ? 'active' : ''}>Meta</span>\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n## Common patterns\n\n### Reading held keys inside a stable callback\n\n`useKeyHold` and `useHeldKeys` return the state for the current render. If a memoized callback reads those values, include them in its dependencies so it sees updates.\n\nFor an event handler that should read the latest held keys without subscribing to render updates, use the existing `getKeyStateTracker()` API:\n\n```tsx\nimport { useCallback } from 'preact/hooks'\nimport { getKeyStateTracker } from '@tanstack/preact-hotkeys'\n\nfunction KeyInspector() {\n  const tracker = getKeyStateTracker()\n  const logHeldKeys = useCallback(() => {\n    console.log(tracker.getHeldKeys())\n    console.log('Space held:', tracker.isKeyHeld('Space'))\n  }, [tracker])\n\n  return <button type=\"button\" onClick={logHeldKeys}>Log held keys</button>\n}\n```\n\nThe tracker is a shared singleton, so its identity stays stable during normal use. Initialize it while setting up the component, before the keys you want to observe are pressed. Read `getHeldKeys()` or `isKeyHeld()` inside the callback; saving their return values outside the callback would save an earlier snapshot. These imperative reads do not subscribe the component to updates. Use the hooks when held keys affect rendering, and do not destroy the shared tracker when a component unmounts.\n\nFor a mouse or wheel handler that only needs a modifier's state for that event, read the event's `ctrlKey`, `shiftKey`, `altKey`, or `metaKey` property directly:\n\n```tsx\nimport { useCallback } from 'preact/hooks'\nimport type { JSX } from 'preact'\n\nfunction WheelInspector() {\n  const onWheel = useCallback((event: JSX.TargetedWheelEvent<HTMLDivElement>) => {\n    if (event.ctrlKey) {\n      console.log('Wheel event with Control modifier')\n    }\n  }, [])\n\n  return <div onWheel={onWheel}>Scroll here</div>\n}\n```\n\nThis reads the modifier state reported by the event. Browsers can also report `ctrlKey` for a trackpad pinch gesture, so it does not necessarily mean the physical Control key is held.\n\n### Hold-to-reveal UI\n\nShow additional options while a modifier is held:\n\n```tsx\nimport { useKeyHold } from '@tanstack/preact-hotkeys'\n\nfunction FileItem({ file }: { file: File }) {\n  const isShiftHeld = useKeyHold('Shift')\n\n  return (\n    <div className=\"file-item\">\n      <span>{file.name}</span>\n      {isShiftHeld && (\n        <button className=\"danger\" onClick={() => permanentlyDelete(file)}>\n          Permanently Delete\n        </button>\n      )}\n      {!isShiftHeld && (\n        <button onClick={() => moveToTrash(file)}>\n          Move to Trash\n        </button>\n      )}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n### Keyboard shortcut hints\n\nDisplay different shortcut hints based on which modifiers are held:\n\n```tsx\nimport { useKeyHold } from '@tanstack/preact-hotkeys'\n\nfunction ShortcutHints() {\n  const isModHeld = useKeyHold('Meta') // or 'Control' on Windows\n\n  if (!isModHeld) return null\n\n  return (\n    <div className=\"shortcut-overlay\">\n      <div>S - Save</div>\n      <div>Z - Undo</div>\n      <div>Shift+Z - Redo</div>\n      <div>K - Command Palette</div>\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n### Debugging key display\n\nCombine hooks with formatting utilities for a rich debugging display:\n\n```tsx\nimport {\n  useHeldKeys,\n  useHeldKeyCodes,\n  formatForDisplay,\n  type RegisterableHotkey,\n} from '@tanstack/preact-hotkeys'\n\nfunction KeyDebugger() {\n  const heldKeys = useHeldKeys()\n  const heldCodes = useHeldKeyCodes()\n\n  return (\n    <div className=\"key-debugger\">\n      <h3>Active Keys</h3>\n      {heldKeys.map((key) => (\n        <div key={key}>\n          <strong>\n            {formatForDisplay(key as RegisterableHotkey, { useSymbols: true })}\n          </strong>\n          <span className=\"code\">{heldCodes[key]}</span>\n        </div>\n      ))}\n      {heldKeys.length === 0 && <p>Press any key...</p>}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n## Platform quirks\n\nThe underlying `KeyStateTracker` handles several platform-specific issues:\n\n### macOS modifier key behavior\n\nOn macOS, when a modifier key is held and a non-modifier key is pressed, the OS sometimes swallows the `keyup` event for the non-modifier key. TanStack Hotkeys detects and handles this automatically so held key state stays accurate.\n\n### Window blur\n\nWhen the browser window loses focus, the tracker clears all held keys. This prevents \"stuck\" keys that would otherwise appear held even after the user tabs away and releases them.\n\n## Under the hood\n\nAll three hooks subscribe to the singleton `KeyStateTracker` via `@tanstack/preact-store`. The tracker manages its own event listeners on `document` and maintains state in a TanStack Store, which the hooks subscribe to reactively.\n\n```tsx\nimport { getKeyStateTracker } from '@tanstack/preact-hotkeys'\n\nconst tracker = getKeyStateTracker()\n\n// Imperative access (also available inside callbacks)\ntracker.getHeldKeys()        // string[]\ntracker.isKeyHeld('Shift')   // boolean\ntracker.isAnyKeyHeld(['Shift', 'Control']) // boolean\ntracker.areAllKeysHeld(['Shift', 'Control']) // boolean\n```\n\n## Modifier-held shortcut hints\n\n`useHotkeyHint` answers whether held modifiers are relevant to a binding. Keep formatting and badge styling in your component:\n\n```ts\nconst visible = useHotkeyHint('Alt+Shift+[KeyK]')\n```\n\nFor `Alt+Shift+[KeyK]`, holding Alt, Shift, or both reveals the hint. An extra Control hides it; releasing all modifiers or blurring the window hides it. Nonmodifier keys are ignored. AltGraph does not reveal hints. Pass `{ exact: true }` to require all binding modifiers, or `{ platform: 'mac' }` to resolve Mod explicitly. Supply the same platform used by the registration when overriding detection.\n\nCombine the boolean with the action's enabled state. The helper does not register a shortcut or determine whether its target is focused. The core equivalent is `matchesHeldModifiers(binding, heldKeys, options)`.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Key State Tracking Guide\nid: key-state-tracking\n---\n\nTanStack Hotkeys includes three hooks for tracking the real-time state of keyboard keys. Use them to show modifier state in the UI or to build hold-to-activate features.\n\n## `useHeldKeys`\n\nReturns a reactive array of all currently held key names.\n\n```tsx\nimport { useHeldKeys } from '@tanstack/preact-hotkeys'\n\nfunction KeyDisplay() {\n  const heldKeys = useHeldKeys()\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      {heldKeys.length > 0\n        ? `Held: ${heldKeys.join(' + ')}`\n        : 'No keys held'}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nThe returned array contains key names like `'Shift'`, `'Control'`, `'Meta'`, `'A'`, `'ArrowUp'`, etc. Keys appear in the order they were pressed.\n\n## `useHeldKeyCodes`\n\nReturns a reactive object mapping held key names to their physical key codes (`event.code` values). This is useful when you need to distinguish between left and right modifiers.\n\n```tsx\nimport { useHeldKeyCodes } from '@tanstack/preact-hotkeys'\n\nfunction KeyCodeDisplay() {\n  const heldCodes = useHeldKeyCodes()\n  // Example: { Shift: \"ShiftLeft\", Control: \"ControlRight\" }\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      {Object.entries(heldCodes).map(([key, code]) => (\n        <div key={key}>\n          {key}: {code}\n        </div>\n      ))}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n## `useKeyHold`\n\nChecks whether a specific key is currently held. This hook is optimized to only trigger re-renders when the specified key's held state changes, not when other keys are pressed or released.\n\n```tsx\nimport { useKeyHold } from '@tanstack/preact-hotkeys'\n\nfunction ModifierIndicators() {\n  const isShiftHeld = useKeyHold('Shift')\n  const isCtrlHeld = useKeyHold('Control')\n  const isAltHeld = useKeyHold('Alt')\n  const isMetaHeld = useKeyHold('Meta')\n\n  return (\n    <div className=\"modifier-bar\">\n      <span className={isShiftHeld ? 'active' : ''}>Shift</span>\n      <span className={isCtrlHeld ? 'active' : ''}>Ctrl</span>\n      <span className={isAltHeld ? 'active' : ''}>Alt</span>\n      <span className={isMetaHeld ? 'active' : ''}>Meta</span>\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n## Common patterns\n\n### Reading held keys inside a stable callback\n\n`useKeyHold` and `useHeldKeys` return the state for the current render. If a memoized callback reads those values, include them in its dependencies so it sees updates.\n\nFor an event handler that should read the latest held keys without subscribing to render updates, use the existing `getKeyStateTracker()` API:\n\n```tsx\nimport { useCallback } from 'preact/hooks'\nimport { getKeyStateTracker } from '@tanstack/preact-hotkeys'\n\nfunction KeyInspector() {\n  const tracker = getKeyStateTracker()\n  const logHeldKeys = useCallback(() => {\n    console.log(tracker.getHeldKeys())\n    console.log('Space held:', tracker.isKeyHeld('Space'))\n  }, [tracker])\n\n  return <button type=\"button\" onClick={logHeldKeys}>Log held keys</button>\n}\n```\n\nThe tracker is a shared singleton, so its identity stays stable during normal use. Initialize it while setting up the component, before the keys you want to observe are pressed. Read `getHeldKeys()` or `isKeyHeld()` inside the callback; saving their return values outside the callback would save an earlier snapshot. These imperative reads do not subscribe the component to updates. Use the hooks when held keys affect rendering, and do not destroy the shared tracker when a component unmounts.\n\nFor a mouse or wheel handler that only needs a modifier's state for that event, read the event's `ctrlKey`, `shiftKey`, `altKey`, or `metaKey` property directly:\n\n```tsx\nimport { useCallback } from 'preact/hooks'\nimport type { JSX } from 'preact'\n\nfunction WheelInspector() {\n  const onWheel = useCallback((event: JSX.TargetedWheelEvent<HTMLDivElement>) => {\n    if (event.ctrlKey) {\n      console.log('Wheel event with Control modifier')\n    }\n  }, [])\n\n  return <div onWheel={onWheel}>Scroll here</div>\n}\n```\n\nThis reads the modifier state reported by the event. Browsers can also report `ctrlKey` for a trackpad pinch gesture, so it does not necessarily mean the physical Control key is held.\n\n### Hold-to-reveal UI\n\nShow additional options while a modifier is held:\n\n```tsx\nimport { useKeyHold } from '@tanstack/preact-hotkeys'\n\nfunction FileItem({ file }: { file: File }) {\n  const isShiftHeld = useKeyHold('Shift')\n\n  return (\n    <div className=\"file-item\">\n      <span>{file.name}</span>\n      {isShiftHeld && (\n        <button className=\"danger\" onClick={() => permanentlyDelete(file)}>\n          Permanently Delete\n        </button>\n      )}\n      {!isShiftHeld && (\n        <button onClick={() => moveToTrash(file)}>\n          Move to Trash\n        </button>\n      )}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n### Keyboard shortcut hints\n\nDisplay different shortcut hints based on which modifiers are held:\n\n```tsx\nimport { useKeyHold } from '@tanstack/preact-hotkeys'\n\nfunction ShortcutHints() {\n  const isModHeld = useKeyHold('Meta') // or 'Control' on Windows\n\n  if (!isModHeld) return null\n\n  return (\n    <div className=\"shortcut-overlay\">\n      <div>S - Save</div>\n      <div>Z - Undo</div>\n      <div>Shift+Z - Redo</div>\n      <div>K - Command Palette</div>\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n### Debugging key display\n\nCombine hooks with formatting utilities for a rich debugging display:\n\n```tsx\nimport {\n  useHeldKeys,\n  useHeldKeyCodes,\n  formatForDisplay,\n  type RegisterableHotkey,\n} from '@tanstack/preact-hotkeys'\n\nfunction KeyDebugger() {\n  const heldKeys = useHeldKeys()\n  const heldCodes = useHeldKeyCodes()\n\n  return (\n    <div className=\"key-debugger\">\n      <h3>Active Keys</h3>\n      {heldKeys.map((key) => (\n        <div key={key}>\n          <strong>\n            {formatForDisplay(key as RegisterableHotkey, { useSymbols: true })}\n          </strong>\n          <span className=\"code\">{heldCodes[key]}</span>\n        </div>\n      ))}\n      {heldKeys.length === 0 && <p>Press any key...</p>}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n## Platform quirks\n\nThe underlying `KeyStateTracker` handles several platform-specific issues:\n\n### macOS modifier key behavior\n\nOn macOS, when a modifier key is held and a non-modifier key is pressed, the OS sometimes swallows the `keyup` event for the non-modifier key. TanStack Hotkeys detects and handles this automatically so held key state stays accurate.\n\n### Window blur\n\nWhen the browser window loses focus, the tracker clears all held keys. This prevents \"stuck\" keys that would otherwise appear held even after the user tabs away and releases them.\n\n## Under the hood\n\nAll three hooks subscribe to the singleton `KeyStateTracker` via `@tanstack/preact-store`. The tracker manages its own event listeners on `document` and maintains state in a TanStack Store, which the hooks subscribe to reactively.\n\n```tsx\nimport { getKeyStateTracker } from '@tanstack/preact-hotkeys'\n\nconst tracker = getKeyStateTracker()\n\n// Imperative access (also available inside callbacks)\ntracker.getHeldKeys()        // string[]\ntracker.isKeyHeld('Shift')   // boolean\ntracker.isAnyKeyHeld(['Shift', 'Control']) // boolean\ntracker.areAllKeysHeld(['Shift', 'Control']) // boolean\n```\n\n## Modifier-held shortcut hints\n\n`useHotkeyHint` answers whether held modifiers are relevant to a binding. Keep formatting and badge styling in your component:\n\n```ts\nconst visible = useHotkeyHint('Alt+Shift+[KeyK]')\n```\n\nFor `Alt+Shift+[KeyK]`, holding Alt, Shift, or both reveals the hint. An extra Control hides it; releasing all modifiers or blurring the window hides it. Nonmodifier keys are ignored. AltGraph does not reveal hints. Pass `{ exact: true }` to require all binding modifiers, or `{ platform: 'mac' }` to resolve Mod explicitly. Supply the same platform used by the registration when overriding detection.\n\nCombine the boolean with the action's enabled state. The helper does not register a shortcut or determine whether its target is focused. The core equivalent is `matchesHeldModifiers(binding, heldKeys, options)`.\n"}
